surface-pro-9-linux
https://github.com/joonhoekim/surface-pro-9-linux

Linux support for the Microsoft Surface Pro 9 with an Intel CPU
(SKU Surface_Pro_9_2038).

This is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, sponsored by or
endorsed by Microsoft, Intel, Realtek, the linux-surface project, the iptsd
project or the libcamera project.

Built on linux-surface
----------------------

The kernel this repository builds is Linux v7.3.4 with the linux-surface patch
series for 7.3 and this repository's patches on top:

  https://github.com/linux-surface/linux-surface
  commit ea852b4eff5ed641571e13766bda5bd9cf121983 (the pin in flake.nix)

linux-surface is not copied into this repository; it is fetched at that commit
when the kernel is built and stays under its own licences.

Patches from other authors
--------------------------

kernel/patches/0001 to 0010 were not written for this repository. They come
from upstream Linux and from pull requests to the linux-surface kernel tree,
as kernel/PROVENANCE.md records patch by patch. They keep their authors and
sign-offs unchanged:

  0001        Sakari Ailus
  0002-0006   Fernando Rimoli (0006 also signed off by Arsalan Naeem)
  0007-0010   Jairo Valdivia

kernel/patches/0028 adds STMicroelectronics' VD55G0 sensor driver (copyright
STMicroelectronics SA, GPL-2.0) as adapted by André Gilerson in pull request
#164 to the linux-surface kernel tree, with changes for the Surface Pro 9 by
Joonhoe Kim.

All kernel patches are licensed GPL-2.0-only, as the Linux kernel is.

iptsd
-----

  https://github.com/linux-surface/iptsd

userspace/iptsd/ holds patches to iptsd (GPL-2.0-or-later); the NixOS module
applies them to the iptsd package of nixpkgs. The touch and pen processing
library helper/crates/sp9-digitizer, used by helper/crates/sp9-digitizerd, derives
from iptsd 3.1.0's processing with those patches, rewritten in Rust for this
device. It keeps
"Copyright (C) the iptsd authors" in the headers of the derived files and is
distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later, which iptsd's "or later" licence permits.

libcamera
---------

  https://libcamera.org

userspace/libcamera/ holds patches to libcamera 0.8.0; the NixOS module
builds libcamera with them. libcamera is not copied into this repository.
Each patch is under the licence of the libcamera files it changes
(LGPL-2.1-or-later, BSD-2-Clause, CC0-1.0), as REUSE.toml records.

